# Shim: re-exports from lib/nogc_sync_mut/src/hash.spl
# Allows `use std.hash.{Hash, hash_combine, ...}` to resolve at runtime
# (previously only `use std.nogc_sync_mut.src.hash` worked, so map.spl's
# `use std.hash.Hash` import was silently inert — see
# doc/08_tracking/bug/primitive_receiver_trait_impl_dispatch_2026-08-07.md)
#
# `src/std` is a symlink to `lib`, so this file WINS the `std.hash` name and
# shadows the pre-existing `nogc_async_mut_noalloc/hash/` package that used to
# answer `use std.hash.{fnv1a_hash_bytes, fnv1a_hash_i64, crc32_byte,
# crc32_bytes}`. Those four symbols are NOT re-exported below yet. The header
# that shipped in b73597bfd03 asserted BOTH "re-exported below" and
# "deliberately NOT re-exported" in adjacent paragraphs; this replaces it with
# the measured truth (tiebreaker run 2026-08-08).
#
# Why not yet, exactly:
#   * The shadowed package annotates its four functions `@noalloc`.
#   * `@noalloc` was never registered in ANY parser/interpreter. The Rust seed
#     interpreter therefore treated it as a Python-style RUNTIME decorator and
#     evaluated the bare identifier `noalloc`, so the module failed to LOAD with
#     `error: semantic: variable noalloc not found`.
#   * That fires on the interpreter path (`bin/simple test`) and NOT on the
#     JIT path (`bin/simple run`) — which is the whole reason two lanes reached
#     opposite conclusions from sound measurements.
#   * Fixed in source 2026-08-08 (`interpreter_eval.rs` decorator skip-list).
#     Verified with a locally rebuilt seed: facade spec 5/5 WITH the re-export.
#
# UNBLOCK CONDITION (dependent work, not a TODO): add
#   export use nogc_async_mut_noalloc.hash.{fnv1a_hash_bytes, fnv1a_hash_i64, crc32_byte, crc32_bytes}
# in the SAME change as, or after, a seed redeploy carrying that fix. Landing it
# before the redeploy poisons `std.hash` for every consumer on the deployed
# binary — including `src/lib/nogc_sync_mut/src/map.spl` (Map/Dict), i.e. most
# of the tree. `src/lib/string.spl` has the identical pending gap for the eight
# `bm_*` symbols in `nogc_async_mut_noalloc/string/mod.spl`, same condition.
# See doc/08_tracking/bug/noalloc_decorator_unbound_in_seed_interpreter_2026-08-08.md
export use nogc_sync_mut.src.hash.{Hash, HashValue, hash_combine, hash_array, hash_tuple2, hash_tuple3, rt_hash_text}

# UNBLOCK CONDITION MET (verified 2026-08-09 against the deployed seed
# built 2026-08-09 04:50:31, which postdates the @noalloc decorator-skip
# fix chain and the 07:45:57 redeploy): `@noalloc` now loads cleanly under
# `bin/simple test` (interpreter path) — probed live with
# `use std.nogc_async_mut_noalloc.hash.mod.{fnv1a_hash_i64}` +
# `fnv1a_hash_i64(42) != 0`, PASS. Re-exporting the four fnv1a/crc32
# symbols per the condition recorded in the previous header revision.
export use nogc_async_mut_noalloc.hash.mod.{fnv1a_hash_bytes, fnv1a_hash_i64, crc32_byte, crc32_bytes}
